From: Nobara Project <nobara@fedoraproject.org>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] x86/split-lock: Default bus-lock detection to 100 locks/sec

Nobara users have encountered complete system hangs while Steam was
generating a sustained stream of bus-lock traps.  The offending instruction
was traced to Valve's libtier0_s.so (the Steam "tier0" library), and the
problem was also observed with Steam's stable, non-beta client.  In one
captured incident, the ThreadedValidat thread generated roughly 4,800-4,900
suppressed handle_bus_lock callbacks every five seconds immediately before
the machine stopped responding -- close to 1,000 bus locks per second.

The upstream warn default reports these events but does not restrict them.
A bus-locked instruction can stall coherent memory traffic outside the
originating core, so a sufficiently aggressive offender can degrade the
whole machine rather than only its own process.  Set a conservative default
of 100 bus locks per second to throttle the task generating the locks while
allowing unrelated tasks to continue running.

Apply this default only when the CPU supports hardware bus-lock detection
and the user did not supply a split_lock_detect= command-line option.  Keep
the existing warn default on CPUs that only support split-lock #AC detection,
since ratelimit mode requires hardware bus-lock detection.  Explicit off,
warn, fatal, and ratelimit:N options retain their existing semantics and take
precedence over the built-in default; in particular, warn removes the limit.

This is intended as a temporary distribution mitigation for the current
32-bit Steam Runtime 1.0 client (steamrt1/scout, observed runtime build
1.0.20260618.246542).  The patch can be removed once Steam's stable channel
moves to the new 64-bit SteamRT3 client (steamrt3c, based on Steam Runtime 3
"sniper") using runtime build 3c.0.20260729.253765 or newer, after confirming
that its libtier0_s.so no longer generates this excessive bus-lock traffic.
---
 arch/x86/kernel/cpu/bus_lock.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/bus_lock.c b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/bus_lock.c
index a75938b..4d37aa1 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/bus_lock.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/bus_lock.c
@@ -46,6 +46,9 @@ static const struct {
 
 static struct ratelimit_state bld_ratelimit;
 
+/* Nobara default; an explicit split_lock_detect= option takes precedence. */
+#define DEFAULT_BUS_LOCK_RATE_LIMIT 100
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_CACHY
 static unsigned int sysctl_sld_mitigate = 0;
 #else
@@ -131,6 +134,16 @@ static void __init sld_state_setup(void)
 				break;
 			}
 		}
+	} else if (boot_cpu_has(X86_FEATURE_BUS_LOCK_DETECT)) {
+		/*
+		 * Limit bus locks by default without forcing a kernel command line.
+		 * CPUs with only split-lock #AC detection keep the warn default,
+		 * because ratelimit mode requires hardware bus-lock detection.
+		 */
+		ratelimit_state_init(&bld_ratelimit, HZ,
+				     DEFAULT_BUS_LOCK_RATE_LIMIT);
+		ratelimit_set_flags(&bld_ratelimit, RATELIMIT_MSG_ON_RELEASE);
+		state = sld_ratelimit;
 	}
 	sld_state = state;
 }
-- 
